# *Dark-Light Insects*

@body

- In the Peppered Moth of insect, fitness is determined by a single gene with two alleles, A and [a]{color=gray}.
  - Allele A causes insects to be dark
  - Allele [a]{color=gray} causes them to be [light]{color=gray}
  - A is completely dominant to [a]{color=gray}.
- Differential survival\:
  - In forests, dark insects (AA and Aa) survive better
  - In open fields, light insects ([aa]{color=gray}) survive better.

=== layout: two-panels

@left

- Differential survival\:
  - In forests, dark insects (AA and Aa) survive better
  - In open fields, light insects ([aa]{color=gray}) survive better.

@right

