=== layout: section

# Directionality of Natural Selection

=== layout: one-panel

# *Natural Selection for Quantitative Traits*

@body

- Fitness can be influenced dramatically by different alleles of a single gene
- but is more often influenced by many genes that affect quantitative traits such as body size, disease susceptibility, and fecundity.
  - [_fecundity &#8211; the ability to produce an abundance of offspring_]{color=#666666}
- Natural selection can affect the distribution of a quantitative trait through
  - directional selection,
  - disruptive selection, or
  - stabilizing selection.

=== layout: one-panel

# *Modes of Natural Selection*

@body

- There are three modes of selection
  - [*Directional selection*]{underline=true} favors variants of a trait at one extreme end of its distribution
  - [*Disruptive selection*]{underline=true} favors both extreme variants of a trait at the expense of intermediate values
  - [*Stabilizing selection*]{underline=true} favors intermediate variants of a trait and acts against extreme phenotypes

