=== layout: section

# Selection-Mutation Balance

=== layout: two-panels

# *Mutation-Drift Balance and Population Size*

@left

- In small populations, genetic drift dominates over mutation.
- In large populations, mutation dominates over genetic drift.

@right

![Slide image 15](assets/lect15c-natural_selection/image_015.png)

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Selection-Mutation Balance*

@body

- Selection acts to minimize the frequency of harmful alleles
  - but never be eliminated because mutation keeps on producing harmful alleles
- So both working in opposite directions, eventually reach state of equilibrium.

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 16](assets/lect15c-natural_selection/image_016.jpg)

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *S-M Equilibrium*

@body

- Equilibrium depends on whether recessive allele is completely recessive or has a small effect (partial effect on the fitness of heterozygotes..)
- If completely recessive, the fitness of (A is wild type and a is recessive allele)\:
    - s = selection coefficient against recessive genotypes
- Selection coefficient measures the fraction of aa genotypes that fails to survive, So equilibrium value
- Selection-mutation balance can be used to estimate human mutation rate.

{table-style=comparison padding="2pt 4pt"}
| Genotype | [AA]{text-align=center} | [Aa]{text-align=center} | [aa]{text-align=center} |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Relative fitness | [1]{text-align=center} | [1]{text-align=center} | [1 &#8211; s]{text-align=center} |

![Slide image 17](assets/lect15c-natural_selection/image_017.svg)

=== layout: one-panel

# *Effect of Degree of Dominance*

@body

- What if the recessive allele is partially dominant, meaning having a small effect on the fitness of heterozygotes
- Then fitnesses of AA, Aa and aa can be written as\:
  - &#8220;[h &#215; s]{color=purple}&#8221; is the selection coefficient against heterozygous carriers
- h &#8211; is called [degree of dominance]{color=red}
  - h = 1 &#8212; harmful allele is completely dominance
  - h = 0 &#8212; it is completely recessive
  - h = &#189; &#8212; heterozygote genotype has a fitness exactly half of homozygous genotypes

{table-style=comparison padding="0.5pt 4pt"}
| Genotype | [AA]{text-align=center} | [Aa]{text-align=center} | [aa]{text-align=center} |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Relative fitness | [1]{text-align=center} | [1 &#8211; [h&#215;s]{color=#55308D}]{text-align=center} | [1 &#8211; s]{text-align=center} |

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

